  <Placemark>
    <name>PCMS – Pacific Crest &amp; Mesoamerica Spine</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>PCMS – Pacific Crest &amp; Mesoamerica Spine</b><br/>6-gleisig (2x Express, 2x Regional, 2x Güter-Transit), ETCS Level 3 Moving Block im relativen Bremswegabstand, 800m-Züge<br/>5.250 km, 10 Std. 23 Min., 9 Zwischenhalte (plus 20 lastfreie Non-Stop-Durchfahrtsbahnhöfe ohne Passagierhalt: Bellingham-North, Everett-East, Tacoma-Dome Bypass, Olympia-South Ring, Eugene-East, Medford-North, Redding-South, Chico-East, Fresno-Central, Bakersfield-North, Anaheim-Transit, Oceanside-Coast, San Quintín, Guerrero Negro, Loreto-Coast, La Paz-North Gate, Tepic-East, Guadalajara-North Bypass, Celaya-Plains, Querétaro-West Bypass). Zeiten in PT/MT/CT vor Ort. Größter Tunnel: Mar-de-Cortés (550 km, Golf von Kalifornien).<br/><br/><b>Beispielfahrt (Stopliste):</b><br/>Surrey (Vancouver): ab 07:00<br/>Seattle-Tukwila Hub: an 07:20 / ab 07:22<br/>Portland-Salmon Creek: an 07:47 / ab 07:49<br/>Sacramento-North Hub: an 09:21 / ab 09:25<br/>Bay Area Mega-Hub (Milpitas): an 09:43 / ab 09:47<br/>Los Angeles-Sylmar Hub: an 10:39 / ab 10:43<br/>San Diego-Torrey Pines: an 11:05 / ab 11:07<br/>Ensenada-North Port Hub: an 11:25 / ab 11:27<br/>Cabo San Lucas-Deep Terminal: an 14:59 / ab 15:03<br/>Puerto Vallarta-East Hub: an 17:28 / ab 17:30<br/>Mexico City-Huehuetoca Hub: an 19:23<br/><style>@media (prefers-color-scheme: dark) { body { background:#1e1e1e; color:#eee; } }</style>]]></description>
